  "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $T$ is the number of elements in $T.$\n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $T:$\n\n$$\n0,\\,{-2,-3,-4},\\,{9,10,11,12}\n$$\n\nNote that ${-2,-3,-4}$ and ${9,10,11,12}$ each count as single elements of $T.$\n\nSince $T$ has $3$ elements, the cardinality is $|T|=3.$",
